<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lucien Bonaparte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1775">1775</a>–<a href="/years/1840">1840</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Lucien Bonaparte was a younger brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>. As president of the Council of Five Hundred he secured the success of the coup of 18 Brumaire in 1799, but he later quarrelled with Napoleon and settled in the Papal States as Prince of Canino. On his estates there he excavated the Etruscan cemeteries of Vulci from 1828, recovering thousands of Greek painted vases.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lucien-bonaparte.jpg" alt="Lucien Bonaparte" width="320" height="409" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: François-Xavier Fabre · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fabre_-_Lucien_Bonaparte.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
